          "date": "2026-11-06 00:45:13.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-19717 tests: use MGS NID in conf-sanity 153b on IPv6",
        "message": "LU-19717 tests: use MGS NID in conf-sanity 153b on IPv6\n\ntest_153b builds its mount strings from the MGS hostname, but\nmount.lustre resolves hostnames to IPv4 only. On IPv6 test\nclusters the client has only an IPv6 LNI, so the resolved\naddress is unreachable and the mount times out. The test fails\non every full-dne-ipv6 run.\n\nUse the MGS NID instead of the hostname when MGSNID is IPv6.\n\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I1a63cd4ef5e54be31deabbfc2a87096f5a9750dc\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
